This additional permission also covers paid or employer-sponsored work
performed solely for these upstream contribution purposes. It does not
authorize use of modified versions for ordinary personal or business
operations, or for providing a separate product or service.

Keep this notice, the base license, and applicable third-party notices with
permitted copies. Clearly identify a contribution fork as unofficial and
link to the official upstream project. Do not present it as an independently
maintained edition, an official release, or an endorsed product.

This permission does not authorize independent development or maintenance
of a downstream edition, general-purpose mirrors, public binary releases,
package-registry or extension-store uploads, rebranding for distribution,
or incorporation of the Software into another project. These exclusions
apply whether the activity is paid or free. Submitting a pull request does
not authorize any of these activities.

You need not finish a contribution, and the upstream project need not accept
it. If work is abandoned or rejected, you may retain its source and review
history as an inactive contribution archive with the notices and upstream
link intact. That archive grants no permission to continue it as a separate
product. Further development is permitted only for a good-faith upstream
